## What is an escrow account??

**Simple:** An escrow account is a **holding account** that keeps money (or assets) safe until certain conditions are met. Nobody can take the money out alone—the rules of the account decide when and to whom it can be sent.

**In this project:** The escrow account is the **address of the LogicSig** (see below). The sponsor sends ALGO/ASA to this address. The account is “controlled” by the TEAL program: the only way to spend from it is by submitting a transaction that the program approves (i.e. the atomic group where both sponsor and organizer sign). So the prize sits in this account until both parties agree to release it to the winner.

**Summary:** Escrow account = the account that holds the prize and only releases it when the contract’s rules are satisfied (here: both sponsor + organizer sign).

